   "gap": "Supply (1) the identification of the reference measure: Durrett's densities on R^n (Exercise 2.1.1, p. 56; Example 4.1.6, p. 209) are taken with respect to his Lebesgue measure on R^d, the measure fixed by the volumes of finite half-open rectangles (Thm. 1.1.11 and Example 1.1.12, pp. 7-8), while the entry uses the product measure lambda^d; that the two coincide (uniqueness from rectangle values, which needs the finite-exhaustion pi-system theorem A.1.5, absent from the route) is not supplied. (2) Durrett's defining form of a real density, F(x) = integral from -infinity to x of f(y) dy (display (1.2.1), p. 12), and its equivalence with the all-Borel-sets form of the entry are not stated on the route.",
